WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.901
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:06.734
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:09.968
-Whew! Sorry.
I'm a little winded.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.968
I'm almost halfway through
blowing up the balloons

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:13.934
for the Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:17.267
And they got Snoopy, they got
Bluey, they got Oppenheimer.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.934
They got a lot of...

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:21.367
Well, guys, everyone
is talking about this.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.467
Today in San Francisco,
President Biden

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.934
met face-to-face with
Chinese President Xi Jinping

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.634
for the first time in a year.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:31.167
Yeah, Biden said,
"Thank you for being here.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.000
And President Xi was like,
"Thanks to TikTok,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.601
I'm always here."

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.934
Well, guys, the House
passed a spending bill

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.634
to avoid a government shutdown,

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.000
and today, it was working
its way through the Senate,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.934
and certain senators actually
spoke up about the bill.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.400
Check out what they had
to say earlier today.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.200
First up,
Senator Mitch McConnell said...

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.033
Then Senator Cory Booker said...

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.801
And Senator Chuck Schumer
said...

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.067
And Senator Joe Manchin said...

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.701
And Senator Tom Carper said...

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:35.267
And Senator Cynthia Lummis
said...

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.234
So Senator Chuck Grassley
said...

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:53.434
Then Senator
Ben Ray Luján said...

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.934
Then Senator
Debbie Stabenow said...

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:13.567
Then Senator
John Fetterman said...

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:23.567
So, finally,
Mitch McConnell said...

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:28.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:31.367
-Wow!
-"Uncle Fester?"

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.868
Switching gears,
after Target announced

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:39.267
that it was going to start
locking up certain items

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.968
to prevent theft,
their C.E.O. said customers

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:45.567
are happy with the company and
are saying a big "thank you."

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.000
That story again.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.067
The C.E.O. of Target
doesn't get sarcasm.

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.267
-Yeah.

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:51.501
-[ Sarcastically ]
Oh, thank you so much.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.601
No, thank you.

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.067
I like having
everything locked up.

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.834
It's fun watching a guy
try 150 different keys

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.400
just so he can buy Q-tips.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.267
Thank you.

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:01.834
He was like, "Yeah,
and so many of them telling me

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:03.067
to go thank myself, too."

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.601
-Oh, wow!

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:08.834
-Did you guys see this?

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:12.267
Google just unveiled a new A.I.
weather-forecasting program

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:14.901
that's more accurate
than existing models.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.701
But it won't be ready to replace
your local weatherman

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:21.634
until it can accidentally
draw dirty shapes on the map.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:25.501
That's the -- Then you know --
Then you know they got it, yeah.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:29.467
"We're just in a little --
Yeah."

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:32.234
"We're expecting some moisture."

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:34.100
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.868
Rain, rain. Rain, rain.
-It's getting nuts out there.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:40.467
-It is just nuts out there.
I don't know.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:45.033
Well, according to this poll,
it's --

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.200
-Eeh!

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.501
-Well, I saw that YouTube is now
requiring creators to disclose

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.234
when they use A.I.
in their videos.

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:53.367
Did you read that?
-Oh!

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:54.734
-Yeah.
It makes sense for YouTube,

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.400
because A.I. has a lot
of people freaked out.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.567
I mean, people are like...

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.367
-[ Screams ]

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:02.300
-I mean, there's so much
we don't know about A.I.,

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.734
and some people think
it has the potential

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.367
to bring the whole Internet
crashing down, kind of like...

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:14.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:22.300
-Happens all the time.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.701
-And for a lot of us, it feels
like A.I. hit us out of nowhere,

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:25.801
kind of like...

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.300
-Bye!
-[ Screams ]

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.567
-Some people want rules
put in place,

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:39.100
because if one small thing
goes wrong now,

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.234
a lot more can go wrong later,
kind of like...

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:45.701
♪♪

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:50.200
♪♪

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:56.100
But other people think
that we should just go for it

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.868
and jump off the deep end,
kind of like...

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.200
-♪ Sail ♪

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.534
Regardless, everyone wants to
know when something is

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:12.501
real or fake, because nobody
likes being tricked,

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:13.868
kind of like...

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:16.167
♪♪
Ah!

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:23.234
Alright. Should have seen
that one coming, yeah.

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:24.434
Some TV news.

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:26.100
CBS just announced
that, after seven seasons,

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.067
"Young Sheldon" is ending.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.234
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:31.400
Yeah. They knew it was time

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.267
when Young Sheldon
was like, "Bazinga!"

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.501
Hey, I read about a new study

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:41.434
that said consuming alcohol
and caffeine together

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.901
could actually lead
to a better night's sleep.

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.901
-Whoa, whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:53.901
♪♪

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:57.334
-It's a phenomenon
that scientists call a coma.

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:02.200
Now whenever I see
a guy chugging

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.968
Red bull and vodka, I think,
"Well, there's a healthy guy."

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:08.367
"Friggin' Jack LaLanne
over there.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.834
Bazinga!"

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:13.601
Hey, guys, I heard about a plane
flying out of New York City --

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:16.734
this is real -- that had to turn
around shortly after takeoff

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:19.267
because a horse
got loose on board.

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:23.067
See? This is exactly
why I always check my horse.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:24.501
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:26.767
Even worse,
when the horse sat down,

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:28.067
it took off its hooves.

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:29.100
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:32.367
It's one of those horses.

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.734
Finally, it's only Wednesday,

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.767
but it feels like so much
has already happened this week,

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.934
and I just want everyone
to remember that every story

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:39.868
has a moral, even news stories.

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:42.300
And sometimes, two stories
can have the same moral.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.467
I'll show you what I mean.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:46.033
It's time for
"The Moral of the Stories."

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:47.901
-♪ It's the moral ♪

